WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.800
Two cups of water at the same temperature.

2
00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:05.860
Two spoonfuls of white crystals.

3
00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:09.840
Stir the first salt into its cup,
and the thermometer reading falls.

4
00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:12.000
The water is getting colder.

5
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.580
Stir the second salt into the other
cup, and the reading rises instead.

6
00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:19.260
Same water, opposite result.

7
00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:24.400
So why do some salts make water colder as
they dissolve, while others warm it up?

8
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:30.200
In this mission, you'll zoom in on a dissolving
crystal and watch what happens to its ions.

9
00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:32.400
Then you'll read the
thermometer like a chemist,

10
00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:35.580
and work out which way the energy flowed.

11
00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:40.520
Your mission: explain why one salt cools
the water while another warms it.